Package: AMRvalid
Title: Population-Aware Evaluation of Antimicrobial Resistance Predictions
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("Md Omar", "Faruqe", , "faruqe@ru.ac.bd", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1226-7226"))
Description: Evaluates antimicrobial resistance (AMR) phenotype predictions
    made by external models and rule-based tools against phenotypic
    reference results, accounting for the population structure of bacterial
    isolates. Provides a documented data contract and input validation;
    classification and probability metrics and antimicrobial susceptibility
    testing agreement metrics (categorical agreement, very major, major and
    minor errors, essential agreement) per species and antimicrobial; checks
    for overlap between training and test isolates; performance by genomic
    distance to the training data; cluster bootstrap intervals and paired
    model comparisons; calibration; prevalence-adjusted predictive values;
    and reports aligned with the TRIPOD+AI checklist (Collins et al. (2024)
    <doi:10.1136/bmj-2023-078378>). Organism and antimicrobial identifiers use
    the classes of the 'AMR' package. Models are not trained inside the
    package.
